/* ============================================================================
binomial-expansion.epher -- expand (a + b)^num: coefficients and terms

The binomial theorem (Newton, 1665; any algebra text): (a + b)^num is the
sum over k of ncr(num, k) a^(num-k) b^k. The built-in ncr gives
the coefficients, which are row num of Pascal's triangle (see pascal-row.
epher). Numeric values: a = 2, b = 3, num = 6, so the expansion is
(2 + 3)^6 = 5^6 = 15625, the check at the end. Everything is exact.

Run it from a terminal:
  Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/algebra/polynomials/binomial-expansion.epher
  Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\algebra\polynomials\binomial-expansion.epher"
  macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/algebra/polynomials/binomial-expansion.epher

The knobs to edit are a, b and num below.
============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs ---------------------------------------------------------------
const a = 2
const b = 3
const num = 6

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
// the coefficients ncr(6, k), k = 0..6: row 6 of Pascal's triangle
for k in 0 to num do ncr(num, k)
// the terms of (a + b)^num, k = 0..6: ncr(num, k) a^(num-k) b^k
for k in 0 to num do ncr(num, k) * a ^ (num - k) * b ^ k
// the same terms summed quietly (a for loop would only echo its collected list)
acc = {0, 0}
while acc[1] <= num do acc = {acc[1] + 1, acc[2] + ncr(num, acc[1]) * a ^ (num - acc[1]) * b ^ acc[1]}
print("sum of the terms:", acc[2])
print("equals (a + b)^num:", acc[2] == (a + b) ^ num)
/* ---- expected output ----
= 2
= 3
= 6
= {1, 6, 15, 20, 15, 6, 1}
= {64, 576, 2160, 4320, 4860, 2916, 729}
= {0, 0}
= sum of the terms: 15625
= equals (a + b)^num: true
*/
